-oriented Junior Buyer to join our team in Sandy, UT. In this entry-level role, you will be on the front lines of our supply chain—managing raw materials, component and packaging purchasing, contract manufacturer relationships, and finished goods inventory across all sales channels.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n  * Procurement & PO Management: Issue and manage purchase orders for raw ingredients, packaging, components, and finished goods. Ensure timely delivery to prevent stockouts across DTC, Amazon, and Wholesale channels.\n  * Vendor & CM Relations: Serve as the day-to-day point of contact for contract manufacturers, suppliers, and packaging vendors. Track production schedules and hold partners accountable to timelines.\n  * Inventory Tracking: Monitor stock levels in Cin7 (ERP) and ShipHero (3PL WMS). Reconcile inventory discrepancies and maintain accurate stock data.\n  * Cross-Functional Collaboration: Partner closely with logistics, marketing, and sales teams to align procurement schedules with upcoming product launches and promotional pushes.\n  * Cost & Quality Control: Assist in tracking supplier performance, verifying invoice accuracy, and identifying cost-saving opportunities for packaging and raw materials.\n\nQualifications\n\n  * Experience: 0–2 years of experience in supply chain, purchasing, inventory management, or a related business field (internship experience counts!).\n  * Software Skills: Hands-on experience with or willingness to learn Cin7 ERP and ShipHero WMS. Proficiency in Google Workspace and Microsoft Excel (data sorting, basic formulas) is required.\n  * Industry Interest: Familiarity or passion for the health, wellness, or dietary supplement industry is a major plus.\n  * Communication & Detail: Strong negotiation skills, excellent follow-through, and exceptional attention to detail.\n\nWork Authorization: Must be eligible to work in the U.S. and commute to our Sandy, UT office Monday through Thursday.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n\n  * Competitive $55,000 annual salary\n  * Hybrid work flexibility (Work-from-Home Fridays)\n  * Deep discounts on Two Birds brand products\n  * Collaborative, high-energy office culture in the Salt Lake valley\n\n  * ### Seniority level\n\nEntry level\n  * ### Employment type\n\nFull-time\n  * ### Job function\n\nPurchasing and Supply Chain\n  * ### Industries\n\nWellness and Fitness Services--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFertilization (https://www.twobirdsoutdoorservices.com/fertilization)\nciteturn4search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Two Birds Outdoor Services provides fertilization as a scheduled service that delivers nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium in ratios matched to your lawn's current deficiencies and seasonal growth demands. ... Effective fertilization depends on matching product formulation to soil conditions and grass type—slow-release formulas provide sustained nutrient availability over several weeks, while quick-release products deliver immediate greening but require more frequent application. ... When should you avoid fertilizing your lawn?\nProfessional application equipment distributes product evenly across the lawn to prevent streaking and burn patterns.\n\nSchedule a lawn evaluation to determine which nutrients your soil lacks and which application timing will produce the most visible improvement.\n\n### What Proper Fertilization Requires\n\nEffective fertilization depends on matching product formulation to soil conditions and grass type—slow-release formulas provide sustained nutrient availability over several weeks, while quick-release products deliver immediate greening but require more frequent application. Application rates must stay within safe ranges because excessive nitrogen causes rapid blade growth that weakens stems and increases water demand, while too little product produces no visible change. Timing matters because nutrients applied during dormancy or extreme heat often wash away or volatilize before grass can absorb them.\n\nAfter fertilization, you'll notice that grass color shifts from pale green or yellowish tones to a deeper, more consistent green as chlorophyll production increases. \nHow does soil pH affect fertilizer effectiveness in Boerne?\n\nAlkaline soils common in the area bind iron and other micronutrients, making them unavailable to grass even after fertilization unless pH is adjusted or chelated nutrients are used.\n\nWhen should you avoid fertilizing your lawn?\n\nApplications during extreme heat above 95 degrees or during drought stress can burn grass because the plant cannot process nutrients efficiently when water availability is limited.\n\nWhy does grass color fade between fertilizer applications?\n\nNitrogen is water-soluble and mobile in soil, so it leaches away with rainfall and irrigation, and grass continuously uses available nitrogen for growth and chlorophyll production.\n\nHow does fertilization work with weed control programs?\n\nHealthy, well-fertilized grass grows thick enough to shade soil and prevent weed seed germination, which reduces the herbicide volume needed to maintain a weed-free lawn.\n\nTwo Birds Outdoor Services applies fertilizer according to soil test results and seasonal growth patterns rather than following a one-size-fits-all schedule. Contact us to arrange a lawn evaluation that identifies which nutrients will produce measurable improvement in your turf density and color.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA Tale of Two Birds Revision Notes — Gujarat 6 | Super Tutor (https://supertutor.in/resources/gj-board/class-6/english/revision-notes/a-tale-of-two-birds/)\nciteturn4search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Quick revision notes for A Tale of Two Birds — Gujarat Board Class 6 English. ... Please make yourself comfortable.' — This is what Bird 2 said. ... Revise formulas and definitions regularly, and use flashcards for quick recall before the exam. ...   * National Education Policy 2020 — education.gov.in\n\nUpdated 6 August 2026\n\nRevision Notes\n\n# A Tale of Two Birds\n\nGujarat Board · Class 6 · English\n\nQuick revision notes for A Tale of Two Birds — Gujarat Board Class 6 English. Key concepts, formulas, and definitions for last-minute revision.\n\n## Key Topics to Revise\n\n1\n\n### Characters in the Story\n\n  * The Mother Bird: A caring bird who lived with her two babies in a tall, shady tree in the forest. She was killed when a heavy branch fell on her during a storm.\n  * The Two Baby Birds: Twin baby birds who looked exactly alike but grew up in very different places and developed very different behaviours.\n  * The First Bird (near the robbers' cave): Grew up hearing the robbers talk. It learned to shout warnings to help the robbers steal from travellers.\n\n2\n\n### Plot Summary – What Happens in the Story\n\n  * A mother bird lived with her two newborn babies in a nest on a tall, shady tree in a forest.\n  * A big storm came with thunder, lightning, heavy rain, and strong wind. Many trees were blown down, including the tree where the birds lived.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicrosoft Word - TeleChartManual.doc (https://videos.worden.com/telechart/telechartmanual.pdf)\nciteturn4search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 18.8 years ago; Now, every time you update your Personal Criteria, two formulas would have to be evaluated.\n\nYou could kill two birds with one stone by using the formula C – C1 (today’s close minus yesterday’s close).\nIf you used the formula above, you would have to create another Personal Criteria called \"Stocks down today\" and use the formula C < C1. Now, every time you update your Personal Criteria, two formulas would have to be evaluated.\n\nYou could kill two birds with one stone by using the formula C – C1 (today’s close minus yesterday’s close). C – C1 will give you the value of the difference between tod